# Request

User: SSE automatic injection worked one or two versions ago and stopped.
Damaged history may be ignored as long as readable IDs are used; remove the
quarantine, archive and history-preservation machinery; deploy locally and to
nightly after real injection is verified.

# Regression (from commit diffs)

- e7d81c7 made begin_attempt scan the whole status file strictly; one
  malformed line anywhere raised and refused every new batch.
- 1b08402 turned that raise into a permanent "delivery_held" in the poller.
- 09017fb also made get(_locked=True) strict, so transitions failed too, and
  added the offline quarantine (generation marker, archive, menu preview).
Walkie's status file has NUL-damaged lines 12888/30025, so every new SSE input
was queued but never submitted.

# Change

- runtime_input_status: no strict mode, no WakeHistoryUnavailable. Undecodable
  lines are ignored (logged once per damage state). A NUL run of any length
  before a complete record is stripped and the record used. A complete record
  at EOF without newline is used; appends add the missing newline first. An
  unreadable file (OSError) raises StatusHistoryUnreadable, a
  ChannelFileLockBusy subtype, so the poll defers instead of resending.
  Past 4 MiB the file is rewritten in place to one latest row per request,
  dropping requests below the queue's lowest remaining id; no archive.
- channel_pending_poll/injection: the history-hold branch is removed.
- Offline quarantine modules, marker and menu row deleted.
- channel_message_repository: no .jsonl.1 archive; damaged rows ignored while
  ids visible in them stay reserved.

Verification, commit and publication are recorded below.

# Source verification

- Isolated exact-file suite (evidence/focused.py, 30 files): 871 tests,
  2 failures, 122 skips (evidence/focused-source.txt). Both failures are in
  test_unisolated_test_guard IsolatedCliAssetTests (isolated codex prompts
  path resolves to ~/.codex) and fail identically on a clean `git archive
  HEAD` tree under the same runner. Pre-existing; cause not investigated here.
- Native claude.exe 2.1.292 acceptance over damaged + NUL history:
  ../../diagnostics/sse-admission-regression/run-claude-final-source-035809
  passed (one socket send per new SSE input, queued/submitted/replied,
  repeat scan sends only the newer input, old submitted/replied/uncertain
  never resent, old bytes unchanged, no archive file). Console text rendered
  to native-screen-rendered.png (labelled; PrintWindow returns empty).
- Protocol-fixture SSE->socket E2E 4/4 (sse-admission-regression/after).
- Real TUI factory in Edge: `session delivery not_blocked | known queued 2 |
  history_observation_partial line 2`
  (../../diagnostics/delivery-health-partial/evidence/final-tui-not-blocked.png).
- ruff (repository), py_compile, check:docs, git diff --check, npm pack
  dry-run (561 files, no recovery modules) passed.
- Published 0.2.51-nightly.20261021-090826.1c0b706 has gitHead
  1c0b706c65ddafe63df6a64454d31e688619f10b; tarball SHA-256
  0f2f3bb15a2d0f9cd07f3a126a69f7c9409ca0c6013bbcb0995fa56f219abe91.
  Fresh snapshot and npm global install each match all 431 Python files;
  removed recovery modules are absent. Installed native acceptance passed
  with the same queued/submitted/replied and no-replay checks. Installed
  focused suite reproduced the same two pre-existing isolation-guard failures
  and 122 skips; no change-specific failure. Installed TUI browser capture
  passed with the partial-history reason visible.

